1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,800
Robot learning teams train on every demonstration they collect.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:14,000
Calibra audits the dataset first: integrity, quality and coverage.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,800
Then it keeps a diverse 25%: quality filter plus greedy max-coverage selection.

4
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:29,800
PushT benchmark: all 165 training episodes vs. Calibra's 41.

5
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:41,800
At 5 to 25% budgets, Calibra subsets stay closer to full-data error than random subsets.

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:51,800
75% less training data. Only 0.8% higher prediction error than full-data training.

7
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:59,000
Have a robotics dataset? Let's test Calibra on it.
